-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[1,4,10,11,12,13,15,18,20,21,28]},{"id":"laban_1803","name":"Laban","also":"","summary":"The son of Bethuel, who was the son of Nahor, Abraham’s brother. He lived at Haran in Mesopotamia. His sister Rebekah was Isaac’s wife (Gen. 24).","verses":46,"father":"Bethuel","mother":"","v":[5,10,13,14,15,16,19,21,22,24,25,26,29]},{"id":"nahor_2143","name":"Nahor","also":"","summary":"A son of Terah, and elder brother of Abraham (Gen. 11:26, 27; Josh. 24:2, R.V.). He married Milcah, the daughter of his brother Haran, and remained in the land of his nativity on the east of the river Euphrates at Haran (Gen. 11:27-32).","verses":10,"father":"Terah","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"rachel_2386","name":"Rachel","also":"Rahel","summary":"Ewe, “the daughter”, “the somewhat petulant, peevish, and self-willed though beautiful younger daughter” of Laban, and one of Jacob’s wives (Gen. 29:6, 28).","verses":45,"father":"Laban","mother":"","v":[6,9,10,11,12,16,17,18,20,25,28,29,30,31]},{"id":"rebekah_2401","name":"Rebekah","also":"","summary":"A noose, the daughter of Bethuel, and the wife of Isaac (Gen. 22:23; 24:67). The circumstances under which Abraham’s “steward” found her at the “city of Nahor,” in Padan-aram, are narrated in Gen. 24-27.","verses":29,"father":"Bethuel","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"leah_1813","name":"Leah","also":"","summary":"Weary, the eldest daughter of Laban, and sister of Rachel (Gen. 29:16). Jacob took her to wife through a deceit of her father (Gen. 29:23). She was “tender-eyed” (17).","verses":32,"father":"Laban","mother":"","v":[16,17,23,24,25,30,31,32]},{"id":"zilpah_3081","name":"Zilpah","also":"","summary":"Drooping, Leah’s handmaid, and the mother of Gad and Asher (Gen. 30:9-13).","verses":7,"father":"","mother":"","v":[24]},{"id":"bilhah_502","name":"Bilhah","also":"","summary":"Faltering; bashful, Rachel’s handmaid, whom she gave to Jacob (Gen. 29:29). She was the mother of Dan and Naphtali (Gen. 30:3-8). Reuben was cursed by his father for committing adultry with her (35:22; 49:4).","verses":10,"father":"","mother":"","v":[29]},{"id":"reuben_2429","name":"Reuben","also":"","summary":"Behold a son!, the eldest son of Jacob and Leah (Gen. 29:32). His sinful conduct, referred to in Gen. 35:22, brought down upon him his dying father’s malediction (48:4).","verses":70,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[32]},{"id":"simeon_2741","name":"Simeon","also":"","summary":"The second son of Jacob by Leah (Gen. 29:33). He was associated with Levi in the terrible act of vengeance against Hamor and the Shechemites (34:25, 26).","verses":40,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[33]},{"id":"levi_1820","name":"Levi","also":"","summary":"The third son of Jacob by Leah. The origin of the name is found in Leah’s words (Gen. 29:34), “This time will my husband be joined [Heb. yillaveh] unto me.”","verses":64,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[34]},{"id":"judah_1751","name":"Judah","also":"","summary":"Praise, the fourth son of Jacob by Leah.","verses":245,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[35]}],"places":[{"id":"haran_527","name":"Haran","kind":"City","lat":36.86,"lon":39.03139,"summary":"Heb. haran, i.e., “parched;” or probably from the Accadian charana, meaning “a road.” A celebrated city of Western Asia, now Harran, where Abram remained, after he left Ur of the Chaldees, till his father Terah died (Gen. 11:31, 32), when he continued his journey into the land of Canaan.","verses":10,"v":[4]}],"events":[{"id":"birth_of_reuben_91","title":"Birth of Reuben","year":-1758,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 29:32. People: Reuben, Israel, Leah.","v":[32]},{"id":"birth_of_simeon_92","title":"Birth of Simeon","year":-1757,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 29:33. People: Simeon, Israel, Leah.","v":[33]},{"id":"birth_of_levi_93","title":"Birth of Levi","year":-1756,"summary":"Passage: Genesis 29:34. People: Levi, Israel, Leah.","v":[34]},{"